<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mississippi River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mississippi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mississippi is the principal river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, draining a vast basin into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>. French explorers travelled it in the seventeenth century and claimed its basin as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, founded at its mouth, became the colony's capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mississippi-river.jpg" alt="Mississippi River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NPS photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Efmo_View_from_Fire_Point.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
